0,Nilotic languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nilotic_languages,"These Nilotic languages' groupings are geographical classifications rather than mutual intelligibility. For instance, the Dinka is a different language from the Luo, which is also different from Nuer etc.Nilo-Saharan branches.","Dinka, Northwestern",Nilo-Saharan
1,"Dinka, Northwestern | Ethnologue Free",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/diw/?cf=1&token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..qcMYrW71RC-FS_LQxhbM5r3iQMJsFxK7G8nFZxh6q7U,Northwestern Dinka is a stable indigenous language of South Sudan. It belongs to the Nilo-Saharan language family and is part of the Dinka macrolanguage. The language is used as a first language by all in the ethnic community.,"Dinka, Northwestern",Nilo-Saharan
